{"call_id": "291aa53979bf4036bf0b21e50987e0a5", "created": "2026-11-23T21:02:57+00:00", "input_hash": "3ba0608636776897c49882975ff188a51ae29ba2dfab9c2d926cedd5fa867f4d", "key": "claude-haiku-5-5|explain/v5|3ba0608636776897c49882975ff188a51ae29ba2dfab9c2d926cedd5fa867f4d", "model": "claude-haiku-5-5", "prompt_version": "explain/v5", "response": {"container": null, "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "Adobe said in its 8-K filed 2025-12-10 that it was ", "type": "text"}, {"citations": [{"cited_text": "“By advancing our innovative generative and agentic platforms and expanding our customer base, we are excited to target double-digit ARR growth in FY2026.”\n\n", "document_index": 0, "document_title": "Promise: 8-K filed 2025-12-10", "end_char_index": 1017, "file_id": null, "start_char_index": 860, "type": "char_location"}], "text": "\"excited to target double-digit ARR growth in FY2026\"", "type": "text"}, {"citations": null, "text": ", and the release stated it targets ", "type": "text"}, {"citations": [{"cited_text": "Exhibit 99.1\n\nInvestor Relations Contact\n\nDoug Clark\n\nAdobe\n\nir@adobe.com\n\nPublic Relations Contact\n\nAshley Levine\n\nAdobe\n\nadobepr@adobe.com\n\nFOR IMMEDIATE RELEASE\n\nAdobe Reports Record Q4 and FY2025 Revenue\n\n•Exceeds target for FY2025 Digital Media ending ARR and targets FY2026 Total Adobe ending ARR to grow over 10%\n\n•Delivers record operating cash flows of over $10 billion in FY2025\n\nSAN JOSE, Calif. – Dec. 10, 2025 – Adobe (Nasdaq:ADBE), the global technology leader that unleashes creativity and productivity for individuals and businesses through innovative platforms and tools, today reported financial results for its fourth quarter and FY2025 ended Nov. 28, 2025.\n\n", "document_index": 0, "document_title": "Promise: 8-K filed 2025-12-10", "end_char_index": 678, "file_id": null, "start_char_index": 0, "type": "char_location"}], "text": "FY2026 Total Adobe ending ARR to grow over 10%", "type": "text"}, {"citations": null, "text": ". The 8-K filed 2026-06-11 lists an updated target of ", "type": "text"}, {"citations": [{"cited_text": "The following table summarizes Adobe’s updated FY2026 targets:\n\nTotal revenue | $26.50 billion to $26.60 billion\nBusiness Professionals & Consumers subscription revenue | $7.44 billion to $7.48 billion\nCreative & Marketing Professionals subscription revenue | $18.21 billion to $18.27 billion\nTotal Adobe ending ARR growth | 10.2% year over year\nEarnings per share2 | GAAP: $17.90 to $18.00 | Non-GAAP: $24.35 to $24.45\n\n2Targets assume non-GAAP operating margin of ~45.0%, GAAP tax rate of ~22.5%, non-GAAP tax rate of ~18.0% and diluted share count of ~399 million for FY2026.\n\n", "document_index": 2, "document_title": "Evidence E6: 8-K filed 2026-06-11", "end_char_index": 1049, "file_id": null, "start_char_index": 469, "type": "char_location"}], "text": "\"Total Adobe ending ARR growth | 10.2% year over year\"", "type": "text"}, {"citations": null, "text": ", and the 8-K filed 2026-09-10 repeats that 10.2% target. In the same September filing, the company reports, as its own figure, that ", "type": "text"}, {"citations": [{"cited_text": "•Total Adobe Annualized Recurring Revenue (“ARR”) exiting the quarter was $27.50 billion.\n\n", "document_index": 3, "document_title": "Evidence E7: 8-K filed 2026-09-10", "end_char_index": 1804, "file_id": null, "start_char_index": 1713, "type": "char_location"}], "text": "Total Adobe Annualized Recurring Revenue (\"ARR\") exiting the quarter was $27.50 billion.", "type": "text"}, {"citations": null, "text": " The status is on track because the FY2026 period has not yet been reported as complete, and the fourth quarter FY2026 targets are still outstanding in that filing.", "type": "text"}], "diagnostics": null, "id": "msg_011ChLXvoHBox5yhQUoXEHw9", "model": "claude-haiku-5-5", "role": "assistant", "stop_details": null, "stop_reason": "end_turn", "stop_sequen